PackageSummary: <text>
Taunicorn is an asynchronous cross-platform local inter-process communication
library for Rust and Python, built around named local endpoints and ordered
full-duplex byte streams.
</text>

PackageDescription: <text>
Taunicorn provides a small transport layer for communication between local
processes. Its Rust implementation is asynchronous and Tokio-based, while the
Python interface is exposed through PyO3.

The transport operates on opaque ordered bytes and intentionally does not
define message framing, serialization, RPC semantics, routing, persistence,
acknowledgements, broker behavior, or application-level delivery guarantees.
Each accepted connection represents an independent full-duplex byte stream.
</text>

